# Every text file is LF in the repo and in the working tree.
#
# Why: this project runs on Windows, and without a rule git warns on every commit
# ("LF will be replaced by CRLF") and silently rewrites files between checkouts.
# That noise hid a real defect once - a blob store that hashed LF but wrote CRLF,
# so content addresses did not match their files (LOG-116). One rule, one encoding.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must not be normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.tei.xml binary
